WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our next guest is a Pulitze
Prize-winning journalist

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
and associate editor
of "The Washington Post."

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
His best-selling book "Rage"
is on sale now.

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Bob Woodward.

00:00:08.541 --> 00:00:11.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
How are you, Bob?
-Well. Thank you.

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.345 line:92%
-Thank you for being here.

00:00:12.345 --> 00:00:16.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
The President had multiple
reactions to your book.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:19.652 align:start size:94% position:6%
Based on the fact that he said
he read it in one night,

00:00:19.652 --> 00:00:22.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
how did you react to what
we think we all know

00:00:22.822 --> 00:00:25.025 size:81% position:41% line:92%
is a very obvious lie?

00:00:25.025 --> 00:00:29.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, maybe he took the
Evelyn Wood speed reading clas

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.098 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the 1970s.
-Yeah, that probably --

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.366 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So, you know...

00:00:33.366 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he has had
varied reactions.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:39.472 align:start size:94% position:6%
He initially said it was
a political hit job.

00:00:39.472 --> 00:00:43.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he said he read it,
found it boring,

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:46.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
"But he said some great things
in it," he said.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:51.885
And then one of the Fox News
anchors actually asked him

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
the key question --
"Is it accurate?"

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:58.058 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said,
"It's okay, it's fine."

00:00:58.058 --> 00:01:01.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which I think is about as
high a praise

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:02.829 size:78% position:39%
as he's going to give
to a book about him,

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:06.666
certainly written by anyon
other than a close friend.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.401
One of the things you asked him,
of course, in the book,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:11.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
is, "Are you worried about
contracting coronavirus

00:01:11.137 --> 00:01:14.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of the way
you are operating

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:15.442 size:84% position:42% line:92%
through this pandemic?"

00:01:15.442 --> 00:01:17.343 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you reflect back on tha
in a week

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:20.280 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he very clearly
did contract it?

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.818 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, he just said,
and it was almost mystical

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:29.756
and we played the tape of it
on television where he said,

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
"No, I don't think
I'm going to get it."

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Why?"
And he said,

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:35.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I just don't think
I'm going to get it.

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:36.596 line:92%
I'm not going to get it."

00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:39.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was said with the kin
of confidence

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:43.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
that obviously has
been not borne out

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.238 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
now that he has it.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:49.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's -- I mean, what I -
I went back and looked

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:53.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
at when we started releasing
those audios,

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:58.017 size:84% position:42%
and you ran one of them
about three weeks ago

00:01:58.017 --> 00:02:00.253 align:start size:94% position:6%
in which he said
back in February

00:02:00.253 --> 00:02:04.858 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it's deadly,
it's deadlier than the flu

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:11.131
and it can be transmitted by
people who don't show symptoms

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:14.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
but very much emphasized
with numbers

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.469 align:start size:94% position:6%
that it's more deadly
than the flu.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:21.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
And now today he says, no,
the flu is more deadly

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.175 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
than the virus.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:25.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course, the numbers totally
contradict that.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:30.950 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he put that up on Facebook
and tweeted it.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.220
And it's interesting, mayb
we've made some progress.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:39.292 align:start size:94% position:6%
Facebook made him take it down
because it's not true.

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:42.228 line:92%
And in the case of Twitter

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
they -- I guess they don't
take things down,

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:47.333 line:92%
but they just say it's false

00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:50.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you can read it
and see that

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:54.607 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Twitter executives
label it false.

00:02:54.607 --> 00:02:57.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know, that, I think,
speaks to one of the trickiest

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:00.046 align:start size:94% position:6%
parts of you writing
a portrait of a president.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:03.750
You mention that he obviousl
tells us all it's the flu.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.486 size:88% position:44%
He tells you privately
it's worse than the flu.

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:10.123
Now he gets it, and he's back to
telling people the flu is worse.

00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:13.426
How do you paint a portrait of
somebody that holds, you know,

00:03:13.426 --> 00:03:17.263
any given position for no longer
than a minute or two?

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:21.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, he does hold
some positions.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.002 line:92%
For ten months his denial

00:03:23.002 --> 00:03:28.241 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the significance of th
virus is very evident.

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
Back in January
they laid it out for him,

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:35.215
told him it will be the
biggest national security threat

00:03:35.215 --> 00:03:37.350 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to your presidency.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.618 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Told him exactly why

00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:41.721 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that the Deputy National
Security Advisor

00:03:41.721 --> 00:03:46.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
had impeccable medical sources
in Hong Kong and China.

00:03:46.793 --> 00:03:49.395 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And he ignored that.

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:51.130 line:92%
He did tell me in February

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:55.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
oh, yeah, that's when he sai
it's going to be worse.

00:03:55.368 --> 00:03:59.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he always said,
"I'm playing it down.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.374 size:78% position:39% line:92%
I'm playing it down."

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:06.613 size:81% position:41%
It was not until May
that I learned that --

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:08.248 line:92%
about the January meeting,

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:13.086
and so when it's in the book
it's a whole picture of hi

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:17.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
avoiding his responsibilit
to protect the public.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.159 align:start size:94% position:6%
One of the first interview
I did with him,

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:23.529
I asked the question, "What'
the job of the President?"

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.732 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he said,
"To protect the people."

00:04:25.732 --> 00:04:29.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
He failed catastrophically
on that front.

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:34.741 size:78% position:39%
President's other job
is to tell the truth.

00:04:34.741 --> 00:04:36.709 line:92%
He failed to tell the truth.

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:39.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what he did in this,
I believe,

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:45.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the record is
so clear and mind-numbing,

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:48.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
will go down in history as
one of the great

00:04:48.588 --> 00:04:51.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
presidential mistakes
of all time.

00:04:51.391 --> 00:04:54.661 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You -- I'm sorry to have to
ask this question,

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
but a friend of mine
wanted me to ask.

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:59.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, don't.
-You won a Pulitzer.

00:04:59.432 --> 00:05:01.968 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does that --
Do you get any money with that

00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
I saw earlier you were --

00:05:05.071 --> 00:05:06.939 line:92%
-I mean, is it just an award

00:05:06.939 --> 00:05:08.207 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is there a little bit
of, you know...

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:09.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Pulitzer Prize
for Watergate was

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.210 line:92%
the Public Service Pulitzer,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:15.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a gold medal
that they give the newspaper

00:05:15.448 --> 00:05:16.516 size:81% position:41% line:92%
"The Washington Post."

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:20.653
So there's -- in some case
that you can't get into,

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:22.121 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is the gold medal.

00:05:22.121 --> 00:05:26.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I didn't get
a share of it.

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:29.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
It rightly went to
the newspaper.

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:31.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
Carl Bernstein and I did
some of the work,

00:05:31.464 --> 00:05:36.002 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we had a great editor,
Ben Bradlee,

00:05:36.002 --> 00:05:40.206 size:84% position:42%
and Katharine Graham,
the owner of the paper,

00:05:40.206 --> 00:05:42.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a very wise lady.

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.677 line:92%
Can I tell a story about her

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:45.411 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Please.

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And she --
After Nixon resigned,

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:55.688 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, oh, it was about just
a few weeks afterwards,

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:58.424 align:start size:94% position:6%
she wrote Carl and myself
a letter,

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:01.561 align:start size:94% position:6%
but she wrote it
on yellow legal pad.

00:06:01.561 --> 00:06:06.833
She had more stationery than any
thousand people in Washington.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:11.204 align:start size:94% position:6%
But this, I think it was
a spontaneous, honest reaction

00:06:11.204 --> 00:06:12.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said,
"Dear Carl and Bob,

00:06:12.805 --> 00:06:15.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
you did some of the stories.
Nixon's resigned.

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:20.313
Now, don't start thinking
too highly of yourselves,

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:23.082 line:92%
and let me give you some advice.

00:06:23.082 --> 00:06:27.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the advice is,
beware the demon pomposity."

00:06:27.387 --> 00:06:30.757 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, wow,
what an important lesson

00:06:30.757 --> 00:06:34.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
for me, for Carl,
people in the media business

00:06:34.827 --> 00:06:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
people in politics,
people in business,

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:41.768 line:92%
even people in show business

00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:43.970 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Pomposity is a demon,

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:48.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it gets in the way
of lots of people

00:06:48.174 --> 00:06:51.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing good work
or their best work.

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.980 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you write a third book
it would also make

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:57.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
one heck of a title
for our President.

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:59.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much.
-The demon pomposity lives

00:06:59.952 --> 00:07:02.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, absolutely.
Thank you so much.

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:04.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-Congratulations on the book

